    "narrative": "As we head into this September 21st slate, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. Facing Yesavage, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside matchup against a 4.57 xERA starter. His profile is bolstered by the 14% SP skill bonus and a favorable batting order position, making him a cornerstone for production across all 5x5 categories. Similarly, **Coby Mayo** earns a Strong classification with a score of 61.78. While his dynamic platoon disadvantage against the right-handed Yesavage slightly dampens his ceiling, the 16% park adjustment and his solidified spot in the heart of the order keep **Coby Mayo** as a reliable option for home run and RBI production.\n\nThe bench decision process today was relatively straightforward due to the schedule congestion, but **Heliot Ramos** hovered closest to the starting threshold before being edged out. With our focus on maximizing the scarce stolen base category, **Heliot Ramos** remains a priority stash, though the current matchup context failed to push him past our 60.00 \"Strong\" start requirement. We continue to monitor the statuses of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and **Kyle Tucker**, who alongside **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**, is unavailable today due to schedule constraints. We are closely tracking the updates for **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, as their late-day availability could necessitate a shift in our strategy to bolster our SB floor. Maintain caution with **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** regarding potential late-game pinch-hit duties, as we look to preserve our remaining game caps for higher-leverage matchups down the stretch.",
